1. Big Data Fundamentals
What is Big Data?

Big Data refers to datasets that are too large, fast, or complex for traditional data-processing systems.

5 V's of Big Data
V	Meaning	Example
Volume	Huge amount of data	TB/PB
Velocity	Speed of data generation	IoT sensors
Variety	Different data formats	JSON, CSV, images
Veracity	Data reliability/quality	Noisy sensor data
Value	Useful information extracted	Business insights
Types of data
Structured
   ↓
Tables, SQL databases

Semi-structured
   ↓
JSON, XML, logs

Unstructured
   ↓
Images, videos, audio, documents
