4. HDFS

HDFS = Hadoop Distributed File System

Used for distributed storage.

Instead of storing:

bigfile.csv

on one machine:

Server 1
   ↓
bigfile.csv

HDFS splits the file into blocks:

File
 |
 +---- Block 1
 +---- Block 2
 +---- Block 3
 +---- Block 4

and distributes them across machines.

HDFS architecture
             NameNode
                |
        -----------------
        |       |       |
    DataNode DataNode DataNode
NameNode

Stores metadata:

File names
Directory structure
Block locations
Permissions
DataNode

Stores the actual blocks.

Important
NameNode → Metadata
DataNode → Actual data
5. HDFS Replication

HDFS normally maintains multiple copies of blocks for fault tolerance.

Example:

Block A

DataNode 1 → A
DataNode 2 → A
DataNode 3 → A

If Node 1 fails:

A still exists
   ↓
Node 2 / Node 3

This is fault tolerance.

