1 2 3 4

Output:

2 4 6 8
filter()
rdd.filter(lambda x: x > 2)
1 2 3 4
      ↓
3 4
flatMap()

map():

rdd.map(lambda x: [x, x])

produces nested results conceptually:

[1,1]
[2,2]
[3,3]

flatMap():

rdd.flatMap(lambda x: [x, x])

produces:

1
1
2
2
3
3
Remember:
map     → one input → one output
flatMap → one input → zero/many outputs
